{"w":2400,"lines":[{"h":0.01453488398216074,"t":"Test 7","x":0.09876543211743273,"y":0.072674418447119415,"c":1,"w":0.061728394826253266},{"w":0.018518517812093099,"y":0.40697674397505423,"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"G","c":1,"x":0.10082304551782177},{"y":0.11686714921530206,"t":"The geography of disease and ill health analyses the frequency with which certain","x":0.14395914572855967,"w":0.77381688435872387,"h":0.018776250531451599,"c":1},{"t":"diseases appear in different parts of the world, and overlays the data with the","y":0.1349951933485154,"h":0.018991252418401161,"x":0.14395528619275144,"c":1,"w":0.72855779012044275},{"c":1,"t":"geography of the region, to see if there could be a correlation between the two.","x":0.14394045926792359,"y":0.15200899680842184,"h":0.020386883451464111,"w":0.74912551879882794},{"x":0.14601443990630297,"y":0.17057636354551819,"h":0.018753852664511683,"c":1,"w":0.73472590128580717,"t":"Health geographers also study factors that could make certain individuals or a"},{"x":0.14609053863809721,"y":0.18895348860258177,"c":1,"h":0.017465828445129006,"w":0.76337448120117191,"t":"population more likely to be taken ill with a specific health concern or disease, as"},{"h":0.019923424692681935,"w":0.73683237711588545,"c":1,"t":"compared with the population of another area. Health geographers in this field","x":0.14599896224054798,"y":0.20600110256063642},{"c":1,"w":0.74074076334635408,"y":0.22526501739076621,"h":0.017467540902720735,"x":0.14609052358524063,"t":"are usually trained as healthcare workers, and have an understanding of basic"},{"y":0.24193606687434044,"h":0.018559009924934644,"t":"epidemiology as it relates to the spread of diseases among the population.","x":0.14602216585272687,"w":0.70588094075520835,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"Researchers study the interactions between humans and their environment that","w":0.75332717895507806,"x":0.14598498866488038,"h":0.020786449400920892,"y":0.26792300313585116},{"y":0.28769140137601212,"w":0.74897120157877606,"c":1,"x":0.14609053123978166,"h":0.016195524146054074,"t":"could lead to illness (such as asthma in places with high levels of pollution) and"},{"x":0.1460204896569193,"c":1,"w":0.761463368733724,"y":0.30503880679464157,"t":"work to create a clear way of categorising illnesses, diseases and epidemics into","h":0.018992135325365589},{"x":0.14403293208043011,"t":"local and global scales. Health geographers can map the spread of illnesses and","y":0.32412790681739478,"w":0.76543207804361979,"h":0.017450420819968948,"c":1},{"w":0.73879923502604172,"h":0.01889989064354769,"y":0.34025518919708664,"x":0.14603311053188178,"c":1,"t":"attempt to identify the reasons behind an increase or decrease in illnesses, as"},{"t":"they work to find a way to halt the further spread or re-emergence of diseases in","x":0.14603051224051361,"y":0.35869291748603094,"w":0.75937296549479161,"h":0.018333253085402568,"c":1},{"h":0.014723203769140047,"t":"vulnerable populations.","w":0.22427983601888021,"y":0.37926972887633492,"c":1,"x":0.14609053457023766},{"c":1,"x":0.14803643055790169,"y":0.40278909936685647,"t":"The second subcategory of health geography is the geography of healthcare","w":0.7224509684244792,"h":0.022056223506500605},{"h":0.022764911359555606,"c":1,"x":0.14792889940132378,"t":"provision. This group studies the availability (or lack thereof) of healthcare","w":0.69791763305664056,"y":0.41934796308820488},{"y":0.44040697659670247,"w":0.77160491943359377,"h":0.016012340046912987,"t":"resources to individuals and populations around the world. In both developed and","x":0.1460905443754037,"c":1},{"x":0.14806016120951512,"h":0.019539563478934929,"y":0.45718303866198462,"t":"developing nations there is often a very large discrepancy between the options","c":1,"w":0.74297968546549464},{"h":0.017467540902720735,"x":0.14814814788199906,"y":0.47526501738741089,"c":1,"w":0.72427983601888013,"t":"available to people in different social classes, income brackets, and levels of"},{"w":0.77983540852864575,"y":0.49411071844963772,"c":1,"x":0.14814813931311402,"t":"education. Individuals working in the area of the geography of healthcare provision","h":0.016195524146054185},{"t":"attempt to assess the levels of healthcare in the area (for instance, it may be very","y":0.51148409913165949,"w":0.76954732259114589,"h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1,"x":0.14814814935455378},{"x":0.14808269158520962,"h":0.018651004674437477,"c":1,"t":"difficult for people to get medical attention because there is a mountain between","w":0.75733245849609376,"y":0.52845356727828141},{"w":0.75124496459960943,"x":0.14805499651464363,"t":"their village and the nearest hospital). These researchers are on the frontline of","y":0.54610661155991302,"h":0.020658372849822748,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.73881947835286454,"t":"making recommendations regarding policy to international organisations, local","h":0.019368509802576761,"x":0.15013720095539052,"y":0.56363964617998452},{"w":0.3006224568684896,"x":0.14802601852177588,"y":0.58386346598079053,"c":1,"t":"government bodies and others.","h":0.016500275323191538},{"y":0.61042402836835474,"t":"The field of health geography is often overlooked, but it constitutes a huge area","x":0.15020575718441612,"w":0.74897120157877606,"h":0.017482948527880904,"c":1},{"t":"of need in the fields of geography and healthcare. If we can understand how","w":0.72038874308268219,"c":1,"x":0.15009261545312758,"y":0.62629314921654189,"h":0.020419844188173442},{"h":0.019207077116230487,"x":0.15013469583537889,"t":"geography affects our health no matter where in the world we are located, we can","y":0.64514255211769955,"w":0.77379130045572919,"c":1},{"y":0.66251154978002624,"w":0.6421635437011719,"h":0.020739549742430197,"x":0.15009769543412099,"c":1,"t":"better treat disease, prevent illness, and keep people safe and well."},{"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"y":0.94622093006049857,"w":0.026748971939086902,"t":"64","x":0.10493827113779536},{"x":0.3946971980310845,"h":0.018255094476526845,"c":1,"t":"leltsresources.org","y":0.96598359624214269,"w":0.2085594177246094}],"h":3395}